--TEST--
`Core\Debug`'s three starts each throw a `RuntimeError` naming the probe when `[debug] mode` leaves it out, even with its path granted, and turn nothing on — `rule:testing/debug-surface`, `rule:testing/debug-mode-directive`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Debug::startTrace
// covers: Core\Debug::startProfile
// covers: Core\Debug::startCoverage
// covers: Core\Debug::coverage
//
// The mode is `[]`, and both sink paths are granted, so the mode is the only
// reason each start below throws. A start that threw a `LogicError`, or none,
// would let a deployment that said "off" be overruled by its own code.
try {
    Core\Debug::startTrace('./out/calls.jsonl');
    echo "trace started\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $error) {
    echo $error->message, "\n";
}
try {
    Core\Debug::startProfile('./out/profile.json');
    echo "profile started\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $error) {
    echo $error->message, "\n";
}
try {
    Core\Debug::startCoverage();
    echo "coverage started\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $error) {
    echo $error->message, "\n";
}

// A refused start created no file. The folder has only the file it started with.
echo Core\Arr::count(Core\IO::list('./out')), " file in the folder\n";

// Coverage never ran, so the result is an empty array.
echo Core\Json::encode(Core\Debug::coverage()), "\n";
--FILE nvs.toml--
[debug]
mode = []

[capabilities.debug]
trace = ["./out"]
profile = ["./out"]

[capabilities.fs]
read = ["./out"]
--FILE out/note.txt--
note
--EXPECT--
Core\Debug::startTrace cannot start, because `[debug] mode` does not include `"trace"`.
help: add `"trace"` to `mode` under `[debug]` in nvs.toml.
Core\Debug::startProfile cannot start, because `[debug] mode` does not include `"profile"`.
help: add `"profile"` to `mode` under `[debug]` in nvs.toml.
Core\Debug::startCoverage cannot start, because `[debug] mode` does not include `"coverage"`.
help: add `"coverage"` to `mode` under `[debug]` in nvs.toml.
1 file in the folder
[]
